<<set $day_step to 7>>
<</nobr>>

Duration: 2 hours 12 minutes
Peak Viewers: 287
Average Viewers: 184
New Followers: 48
Total Followers: 300
Donations: $220.00
Subscribers: 14

Three hundred followers. The number has a roundness to it, a completeness, a milestone that would have seemed impossible four days ago when EliPlays had 54 and a troll and a dream that smelled like microwave burritos. Three hundred people following a pair of eyes and a voice and a name. Three hundred people who will be notified tonight when those eyes return with a nose beneath them.

$220 this morning. Total ElliePlayz earnings: $876.

The brow sculpt debt is $300. The nose is $500. $876 covers both with $76 surplus, which means I'm still short if I pay both today. But the morning stream just earned $220 and tonight's stream will earn at least that much if the pattern holds. The math is tight but it works.

I close OBS. Take off the wig. Eli returns in the dead preview. Pale. Male. The lashes and brows that look strange without their context, feminine accessories on a masculine frame, like finding a tiara on a construction worker.

11:30 AM. Two and a half hours until RegenaForm.

I pick up the phone. Call Marcus.

<<set $hint to "Call Marcus">>
[[Call Marcus|day_5_8_kira]]


:: day_5_8_kira
<<set $day_step to 8>>
<<set $hint to "Call Marcus">>

The phone rings twice. Marcus picks up with the sound of something metallic in the background   the phone repair shop, machines and screwdrivers and the ambient buzz of cracked screens being resurrected.

<<marc "Yo. I'm at work.">>

<<eli "Can you talk?">>

<<marc "Devon just dropped a customer's watch into a cleaning solution that was definitely not for watches, so yeah, there's a distraction. What's up?">>

<<eli "You know how you said the streaming stuff was going better?">>

<<marc "Yeah.">>

<<eli "It's going a lot better.">>

<<marc "Define a lot.">>

<<eli "Like... actually making money. Real money. Not three-fifty money.">>

A pause. I can hear Marcus processing   the recalibration of expectations, the mental shift from "Eli's delusional hobby" to "Eli's delusional hobby might be working."

<<marc "How much real money are we talking?">>

<<eli "Enough to buy lunch. Real lunch. For myself.">>

<<marc "Bro.">>

<<eli "I know.">>

<<marc "You haven't bought your own lunch since... have you ever bought your own lunch?">>

<<eli "I bought a gas station sandwich in September. But this would be actual food. From a place with tables.">>

<<marc "I'm proud of you and also deeply suspicious. What changed?">>

<<eli "New approaches. Like I said. Content strategy. Timing.">>

I hear him deciding whether to push. The pause that means Marcus is weighing curiosity against respect, the internal calculation he runs every time I offer an incomplete answer. He's gotten three of these now   "streaming stuff," "new approaches," "content strategy"   and each one is a brick in a wall he can see me building.

<<marc "Okay. I'm glad, man. You deserve a win.">>

<<eli "Thanks, Marc.">>

<<marc "Saturday still on for Rift Walkers?">>

<<eli "Hundred percent. Floor 17.">>

<<marc "Floor 17. We're coming for it.">>

<<eli "Also   Marc?">>

<<marc "Yeah?">>

<<eli "Thanks. For everything. The curry and the cheese puffs and the coffee and the... all of it.">>

He's quiet for a second. Marcus is never quiet for a second unless something landed.

<<marc "Bro. You good?">>

<<eli "I'm good. I just wanted to say it.">>

<<marc "...you're freaking me out a little. But okay. Love you too, weirdo. Gotta go, Devon's crying.">>

<<eli "Is the watch okay?">>

<<marc "The watch is dead. The customer is outside. Devon is barricaded in the back room. Tuesday energy on a Friday.">>

<<eli "Good luck.">>

<<marc "Luck isn't enough. I need a new coworker.">>

He hangs up. The apartment is quiet. The call sits in my chest the way Marcus always sits in my chest   steady, warm, the ballast that keeps me upright when everything else tips. I said thank you. Out loud. On the phone. Like a person who has the emotional vocabulary for gratitude, which I didn't a week ago, which I'm building alongside the face and the follower count and the shampoo habit.

I put the phone down.

<<set $hint to "Order brunch">>
[[Order food|day_5_9_kira]]


:: day_5_9_kira
<<set $day_step to 9>>
<<set $locationName to "Eli's Apartment">>

Brunch. Real brunch. Not a microwave burrito   actual food, ordered with actual money, delivered to my actual door by an actual human being on an actual bicycle.

I open a delivery app. The interface is familiar   I've scrolled through it before, hundreds of times, the way you scroll through a luxury car website when you ride the bus. Browsing as fantasy. Prices that existed in a currency I didn't have, menus that described a life I wasn't living.

Today the prices look different. Today they look like numbers instead of barriers.

I order from a place called Morning Glory   a breakfast spot six blocks away that I've walked past a hundred times and never entered. An egg sandwich with avocado and pickled onion on a brioche bun. A side of seasoned potatoes. A coffee   real coffee, not Monster Energy, not the cheap grounds I heat on the hot plate, but a latte. Oat milk. Large.

The total is $23.47 with delivery and tip.

Twenty-three dollars. That's roughly eleven minutes of streaming as Ellie, based on yesterday's per-hour rate. Eleven minutes of performing to fund one meal. The math makes the meal feel earned in a way that Marcus's bought coffees and Kira's treated ramen never did. Not because their generosity was wrong   because this is mine. My money. My meal. My eleven minutes of a manufactured voice turned into avocado and pickled onion and oat milk.

The food arrives twenty-two minutes later. A knock on the door. A paper bag. The delivery person doesn't look at my face   nobody ever looks at my face   and I take the bag and close the door and stand in my apartment holding the first meal I've bought for myself in longer than I can calculate.

I sit at the desk. Unwrap the sandwich. The brioche is golden and slightly warm and the avocado is ripe and the egg yolk is just runny enough to pool in the bottom of the wrapper when I bite and the pickled onion gives it a sharpness that cuts through the richness. The potatoes are crispy and seasoned with something herbal that I can't identify because my palate has been calibrated by eight months of microwave burritos and the subtlety of actual seasoning is a language I'm relearning.

The latte is good. Genuinely good. The oat milk froths into a texture that's smooth and sweet and I drink it slowly, sitting at my desk, looking at the morning's dashboard   $220, 300 followers   and the meal tastes like proof. Proof that the numbers translate. Proof that the voice and the name and the wig and the lashes convert into something tangible, something I can hold, something warm in my hands that isn't a Monster Energy can.

I eat everything. Every potato. Every drop of yolk. I drain the latte and set the cup beside the monitor and look at it   the empty paper cup with the Morning Glory logo, a sun rising over a coffee bean   and I feel full. Not just physically. Full in the way that a person feels full when they've done something for themselves without asking permission or assistance or apologizing for the cost.

$23.47 well spent. The best eleven minutes of streaming I've ever invested.
<<set $money -= 23.47>>
12:45 PM. Appointment at 2:00. Time to get ready.

I shower again   bar soap this time, no shampoo, but the hair is clean enough from this morning. Grey shirt. Joggers. Hoodie. Sneakers. The uniform. But the person wearing it has a latte in his bloodstream instead of Monster Energy and the difference is chemical and philosophical and visible in the way I stand, slightly straighter, slightly less like a question mark with shoes.
<<set $hint to "Go to RegenaForm">>
[[Go to RegenaForm|neighbourhood]]

:: day_5_10_kira
<<nobr>>
<<set $day_step to 10>>
<<set $locationName to "RegenaForm Clinic">>
<</nobr>>

The walk to Suite 12 takes twelve minutes. Four blocks. Same route as two days ago   past the laundromat, past the corner store, past the bail bondsman who shares a building with the clinic that's rebuilding my face. January is holding, the cold stubborn and dry, but I barely feel it. The hoodie does its thing. The sneakers crunch on sidewalk salt. I walk with purpose   not the shuffling, head-down, hood-up gait of the old Eli, the one who moved through the world like he was apologizing for occupying space. I walk like a person with a 2 PM appointment and $876 in earnings and a plan.

The frosted glass door. The chrome helix. Suite 12.

Lina is behind the desk. Same dove-grey dress, same amber-gold eyes, same smile that's warm and practiced and exists in the exact center of the uncanny valley between genuine and manufactured. She looks up when I enter and the smile deepens by a fraction   recognition, the specific warmth reserved for returning clients.

<<lina "Ellie! Welcome back. We've been expecting you.">>

<<eli "Hey, Lina.">>

<<lina "Dr. Voss is prepping for your procedure. Can I get you anything while you wait? We have a new green tea   matcha, very smooth.">>

<<eli "Sure. Thanks.">>

She pours the tea from a ceramic pot into a cup that probably costs more than my desk chair. I take it and sit on the grey couch   still rigid, still beautiful, still uncomfortable in the way luxury furniture often is   and sip. The matcha is good. Everything in this clinic is good. That's the trap and the treatment simultaneously.

<<eli "Also   I want to settle the brow sculpt balance. The three hundred.">>

<<lina "Of course.">>

She pulls up my account on the tablet behind the desk. Taps. The interface glows   my profile, my procedures, my balance. $300 outstanding. Due in two days.

<<eli "Can I pay that now? and put the nose on the same credit arrangement?">>

<<lina "Absolutely. The brow sculpt balance   three hundred   cleared today. The nose refinement   Slope, five hundred   would be on a seven-day credit window, same terms. Does that work?">>
<<set $money -= 300>>
<<eli "That works.">>
<<set $loan        to 0>>
She processes the payment. $300 deducted from my streaming payout. The debt that's been sitting on my chest like a second splinter dissolves. Paid. Cleared. My first real financial obligation met with money I earned, not money Marcus lent or Kira treated or my mother Venmo'd. Mine.

<<lina "The nose procedure is confirmed at five hundred. Seven-day window. You'll have that covered in no time at the rate you're going.">>

She says it like she knows my rate. She probably does. RegenaForm knows everything   the earnings, the growth trajectory, the exact moment I could afford each tier. The concierge at the door.

<<lina "Dr. Voss is ready for you.">>

[[Go to the procedure room|day_5_11_kira]]

:: day_5_11_kira
<<nobr>>
<<set $day_step to 11>>
<<set $hint to "The nose procedure">><</nobr>>
The procedure room. Same reclining chair. Same adjustable lights. Same tray of instruments I can't identify. Dr. Maren is standing beside the chair, the lab coat crisp, the helix pin catching the overhead light, the grey-green eyes already on my face when I walk in. Reading. Always reading.

<<dr_maren "Ellie. Good to see you again. How have the lashes and brows settled?">>

<<eli "Perfect. They're   yeah. They're great.">>

<<dr_maren "I can see. The brows have reached their full arch. Excellent integration. Your cells respond well to the treatment.">>

They gesture toward the chair. I sit. Recline. The ceiling is white and crackless and wrong.

<<dr_maren "Today we're addressing the nose. Slope refinement   narrowing the bridge, softening the tip, correcting the asymmetry. The procedure takes approximately forty minutes. Same process as before   bioactive compound, your own DNA template, the cells restructuring in real time. You'll feel warmth at the application site. Full refinement completes in two to three hours.">>

<<eli "And the result?">>

<<dr_maren "Your nose is currently one of the primary masculine tells on your face. The wide bridge, the rounded tip   these read as male to the observer's eye, usually in the first half-second. The Slope refinement narrows the bridge by approximately three millimeters per side, straightens the profile line, and softens the tip from rounded to gently angled. The result will read as neutral to feminine depending on context. On camera, with the framing you've been using, it will integrate seamlessly with the lash and brow work.">>

They tap the wall screen. My face appears again   high resolution, merciless, the clinical lighting finding every flaw. But the face looks different than it did two days ago. The lashes frame the eyes. The brows lift the forehead. The modifications I've already made create a foundation that makes the remaining masculine features   nose, jaw, lips   stand out more by contrast. The face is a renovation half-complete, the beautiful new paint on the upper walls making the scuffed floors more visible.

The digital overlay activates. The nose morphs   the bridge narrowing, the tip refining, the asymmetry correcting. The change is subtle and seismic. The face on screen with the modified nose looks not just different but resolved   as if the nose was the missing puzzle piece, the bridge between the feminized upper face and the still-masculine lower face. With the nose done, the crop line can drop. The webcam can show eyes plus nose. The viewers will see a face that's two-thirds feminine and the remaining third   jaw, lips   will be the next project.

<<dr_maren "Shall we begin?">>

<<eli "Yeah. Let's go.">>

They apply the compound. Cool gel on the bridge of my nose, across the tip, along the sides where the nostrils meet the cheek. Then warmth   deeper than the lashes, deeper than the brows. The nose has more structure, more cartilage, more architecture to reshape. The warmth penetrates into the bone, into the bridge, into the places where the face's infrastructure lives.

I close my eyes. Forty minutes.

I think about Kira. About tonight. About the gyudon and the apartment and the truth I'm going to tell her. I rehearse the words in my head the way she rehearsed her confession in the shower   practicing, refining, trying to find the sequence that explains without excusing, that confesses without begging, that tells the truth without losing the person I'm telling it to.

Kira, I need to tell you something.

Too ominous. She'd panic.

Kira, you know how you said the system can be hacked?

Better. Starts with her. Starts with the shared knowledge.

I found a way. The voice modulator. A new account. A different name and it worked   Kira, it worked so fast it scared me and then I came here   to this clinic   and they changed my face. Not all of it. The lashes and the brows you noticed and now the nose. Today. Right now, while you're buying groceries for gyudon, someone is reshaping my nose four blocks from my apartment because the streaming economy pays for a face I'm building instead of the one I was born with.

Too long. Too much at once. She'd overload.

Kira, I'm Ellie.

Three words. Nuclear. But accurate.

The warmth continues. I feel the reshaping   not pain, not exactly, but the awareness of change. The cartilage shifting. The bridge narrowing millimeter by millimeter. The tip losing its roundness, gaining an angle, softening from something that reads as male into something that reads as a question the viewer answers with "female" because the lashes and brows and hair have already primed the answer.

<<dr_maren "The structural work is complete. Opening your eyes.">>

[[See the new nose|day_5_12_kira]]

:: day_5_12_kira
<<nobr>>
<<set $day_step to 12>>
<<set $hint to "See the new nose">>
<<set $appearance to 6>>
<<set $femininity to 4>>
<<set $confidence to 4>>
<<set $loan        to 500>>
<<set $playerImage = "images/user/tier_1_4.jpeg">><</nobr>>

I open my eyes. Dr. Maren holds the mirror.

The nose is   different. Immediately, visibly, undeniably different. The wide bridge that dominated the center of my face for twenty-two years has narrowed. The rounded tip that gave the whole feature its blunt, masculine quality has refined into a gentle downward slope   the kind of nose that doesn't demand attention but directs it, a feature that serves the face rather than occupying it. The asymmetry is gone. The bridge runs straight, the profile clean, the nostrils proportional and tucked.

Combined with the lashes and the brows, the effect is 

I stare at my reflection. The face in the mirror is crossing a line. The upper two-thirds   forehead, brows, eyes, nose   now read as feminine. Not ambiguously, not questionably, but actually, measurably feminine. A stranger seeing this face from the forehead to the upper lip would identify it as female. The bone structure, the brow arch, the lash density, the refined nose   they compose an image that the viewer's brain categorizes without hesitation.

The lower third   the jaw, the lips, the chin   is still Eli. Still masculine. The flat undefined jawline, the thin pale lips, the shadow of stubble that no amount of bioactive compound has addressed yet. The face is a painting completed from the top down, the artist's brush stopping mid-canvas, the upper half gallery-ready and the lower half still in sketch.

But from the nose up. In the webcam frame. With the wig.

<<dr_maren "The Slope refinement. The bridge will continue settling for two to three hours   you'll notice the definition sharpen over the afternoon. By this evening, the nose will be at its final state. Take care not to press or impact the bridge during the settling period.">>

<<eli "It's   it looks ">>

<<dr_maren "Like you. Just more so.">>

The same line from last time. The same gentle insistence that they're not changing me, not creating someone new, just "unlocking" what was always there. The marketing and the medicine, indistinguishable, a double helix of sell and heal.

<<eli "Can I see it with the wig?">>

<<dr_maren "Of course. Lina?">>

[[Wig fitting room|day_5_13_kira]]

:: day_5_13_kira
<<nobr>>
<<set $day_step to 13>>
<<set $playerImage = "images/user/tier_1_5.jpeg">><</nobr>>
Lina leads me to the fitting room. The lit vanity mirror. The wig forms on the wall. She selects my StreamLine wig   the brownish-auburn waves, the one I've been wearing for three days, the one that lives on a care form in my closet beneath the pile of clothes where the rod fell.

She puts it on me. The practiced routine   tuck, position, align, secure. Her vanilla-and-linen hands adjusting the lace front with impersonal precision.

<<lina "There.">>

I look in the mirror.

The person looking back at me is not Eli. The person looking back at me is not quite Ellie either   not the full Ellie, not the face reveal Ellie, not the version the viewers are building in their imaginations from a pair of eyes and a voice. But the person in the mirror is closer to Ellie than Eli has ever been.

The wig frames the face. The lashes anchor the eyes. The brows arch softly and now the nose   the Slope nose, narrow and straight and gently angled   sits at the center of the composition like a keystone, the element that connects the feminized eyes to the still-masculine mouth and makes the upper face read as coherent. Complete. A girl's eyes above a girl's nose above a jawline that still needs work but can be hidden, cropped, managed.

From the eyes to the nose. The crop line drops. The webcam can show more. Tonight, the viewers will see Ellie's eyes AND Ellie's nose and the face that emerges will be real   not AI, not a filter, not a projection. Real lashes, real brows, real nose, real skin. The lie built entirely from truth.

I stare for ten seconds. Fifteen. Lina waits, patient, the smile holding.

<<lina "The refinement suits you. The proportions are harmonizing beautifully.">>

<<eli "Thank you.">>

<<lina "Dr. Voss wanted me to mention   the next logical step in the Tier 1 progression would be lip enhancement. Natural-Full. Four hundred Dollars. But there's no rush. The nose alone will make a significant difference to your framing.">>

The upsell. Always the upsell. The next step mentioned casually, a seed planted in the fertile soil of visible progress. But I barely hear it. I'm looking at the mirror and the mirror is showing me a version of myself that I   I don't know what I feel. The feeling doesn't have a name. It's not pride, not exactly. Not disgust, not exactly. It's something in between, something new, the specific emotion of watching your own face become someone else's and recognizing both versions as yourself.

I take off the wig. Hand it to Lina. The face returns to Eli   but a different Eli than five days ago. An Eli with long lashes and arched brows and a straight, narrow nose that doesn't match the jawline or the lips but does match the direction. The direction is feminine. The direction is Ellie. The direction is money.

<<eli "Thanks, Lina. I'll think about the lips.">>

<<lina "Of course. We're always here.">>

She says "always" the same way MidnightWhale99 says "always." The certainty of a system that knows you'll return because the loop requires it.

I leave the clinic. The January air hits the new nose   the cold felt differently on the narrowed bridge, the sensation of air moving through refined nostrils, the physical novelty of a feature I've had my entire life suddenly being different. I touch it, gently, the way you touch something expensive. The bridge is smooth. Straight. Narrow. The tip is softer than the original, gently angled instead of rounded. It feels like someone else's nose on my face.

It feels like Ellie's nose on Eli's face.

Four blocks home. I walk with the hood up, not because I'm hiding but because the nose needs to settle and the cold isn't helping. In my pocket, the phone buzzes.

<<kira "groceries acquired! i bought SO much rice. we're going to be eating rice for a week. what time are you coming?">>

<<eli "6ish. also i'm bringing something">>

<<kira "bringing what??">>

<<eli "you'll see">>

<<kira "eli. what are you bringing.">>

<<eli "trust the process">>

<<kira "you sound like a life coach and it's scaring me 😂">>

<<kira "see you at 6 disaster ❤️">>

<<eli "❤️">>

The red heart. Sent with the knowledge that in approximately four hours I'm going to tell her everything. The heart might be the last one I send from the simple side of the truth. The next one   if there is a next one   will be sent by a person she knows fully instead of a person she knows partially.

The thought terrifies me. The thought also feels, for the first time, like the right thing.

<<set $hint to "Go home and prepare for tonight (Bedroom)">>

<<link "Go Home">>
<<set $playerImage = "images/user/tier_1_4.jpeg">>
<<goto "neighbourhood">><</link>>

:: day_5_14_kira
<<nobr>>
<<set $day_step to 14>>
<<set $hint to "Prepare for Kira">>
<<set $locationName to "Eli's Apartment">>
<<set $locationImage to "images/locations/eli_apartment.jpeg">>
<</nobr>>

4:30 PM. Two hours and counting.

The nose has settled. I can feel it   or rather, I can feel the absence of what was there before. The wide bridge, the asymmetric roundness, the thing I avoided looking at for twenty-two years. Gone. Replaced by something narrow and straight and gently angled, something that sits on my face like it was always supposed to be there, like the original was the rough draft and this is the published version.

I stand in the bathroom mirror. The overhead light flickers its death rattle. In the bad lighting, in the yellow-white strobing of a bulb that should have been replaced months ago, my face looks   assembled. The lashes, the brows, the nose. Three modifications, three steps down a road that stretches further than I can see. The upper face is Ellie's. The lower face is Eli's. The nose bridges the two like a hyphen between names.

I'm going to tell her.

The resolution hasn't faded. It hardened over the afternoon, calcifying from intention into commitment the way the nose calcified from gel to cartilage. I rehearsed the words while the food digested and the nose settled and the clock ticked toward 6 PM. Different versions. Different openings. Different strategies for saying the same unsayable thing.

I settle on honesty. Not the crafted kind   not the "Kira, you said systems can be hacked" kind that uses her own logic as a shield. Raw honesty. The kind that doesn't have a strategy. The kind that stands in the open and waits to be shot at.

But first: the something I'm bringing.

I put on my shoes and walk four blocks in the opposite direction from RegenaForm, to the row of shops near the main road. A convenience store. A dry cleaner. A florist.

A florist.

Marcus said bring flowers. Marcus who's never been on time for anything in his life but who has never been wrong about a single emotional observation he's made about me in two years.

The florist is small, wedged between a nail salon and a cell phone accessories shop. The inside smells like earth and water and something sweet that I can't identify. There are arrangements in buckets   roses, lilies, sunflowers, things with names I don't know. The woman behind the counter looks at me with the patient tolerance of a person who has seen every kind of clueless man walk through that door.

<<eli "I need flowers. For a   for someone.">>

The woman nods. Doesn't ask who. Probably doesn't need to.

I scan the buckets. Roses feel too heavy   too much symbolism, too much pressure, too many romantic comedies stacking meaning onto a flower that just wants to be a flower. Sunflowers feel too casual. Lilies feel like a funeral.

There's a bucket of small flowers I don't recognize   delicate, white and pale pink, clustered on thin stems. They look like the kind of thing you'd see in a field in a Studio Ghibli movie. Simple. Unpretentious. Beautiful without trying.

<<eli "What are those?">>

The woman looks. "Sweet pea. They mean gratitude. Also 'thank you for a lovely time.'"

Gratitude. Thank you for a lovely time. For picking me up in a Honda Civic that smells like cherry blossom. For buying me ramen and saying "you have me" across a table. For falling asleep on my shoulder and not caring that I couldn't move for forty-five minutes. For being honest about the system and kind about the gap and patient with the coward who laughed off calling you hot and then, four days later, didn't.

<<eli "Those. Please.">>
<<set $money -= 14>>
She wraps them in brown paper. Ties them with twine. $14. I pay with money that Ellie earned and Eli is spending and the loop completes another revolution.

I walk back to the apartment. Shower, quick. Bar soap. The grey shirt   but I also have a clean black t-shirt, the one that's "least stained," and tonight I choose the black. Not the grey. Something slightly closer to intention. I push the hair back from my forehead   the hair that's clean but missing the Marriott luster   and look in the mirror.

The face. The new face, the half-finished renovation. The lashes and brows and nose that read feminine from above and the jaw and lips that read masculine from below. In the bathroom light it's a face in transition and in the right context, with the right framing, the transition could go either direction.

Kira is going to see this face. Up close. Four inches away, the distance she studies things from, the distance where the freckle near her eyebrow becomes visible and the world narrows to two faces and the space between them.

She's going to see the nose.

She'll notice. She always notices and this time, when she says "hmm" or "did you do something?" I'm not going to say skincare routine. I'm not going to say grooming kit. I'm not going to lie.

I grab the flowers. The keys. The hoodie. The crushed sneakers that have walked me to a clinic and back three times now, four blocks each way, the distance between the person I was and the person I'm becoming measured in city blocks and StreamCoin.

6:00 PM. I text Kira.

<<eli "on my way. buzzing in 15">>

<<kira "door's open! also packet is judging the gyudon. he keeps sniffing the pot and looking at me like i've betrayed him by not making it cat-flavored">>

<<eli "cat-flavored gyudon is a niche market">>

<<kira "don't give him ideas 😤">>

I walk. Fifteen minutes. The January evening is settling, the grey-blue dusk thickening into dark, the streetlamps flickering on one by one. The flowers in my hand feel conspicuous   a man with sweet peas in brown paper walking through a cold city toward a girl's apartment. A man with a new nose and a secret and a bundle of gratitude-flowers and a speech he hasn't finished rehearsing.

<<set $hint to "Go to Kira's apartment">>
