I close OBS. Close VoxMorph. Take off the wig. The face returns to Eli   but a different Eli than yesterday, a different Eli than last week. An Eli with lashes and brows and a straight nose that doesn't match the jaw or the lips but doesn't need to because the jaw and the lips aren't on camera and the person who matters most already knows.

Kira knows.

The thought settles into my chest and the place where the splinter lived is   not empty. Not healed. But quieter. The splinter didn't vanish when I told the truth. It relocated. From "I'm hiding this from the person I love" to "the person I love knows and she stayed." The guilt is smaller now. The warmth is bigger. The ratio has shifted.

I check my phone.

<<kira "how did the nose stream go?">>

<<eli "347 peak. 252 in donations. they called it nose reveal night">>

<<kira "NOSE REVEAL NIGHT 😂 that's iconic">>

<<eli "midnight whale said the face is being built like a cathedral">>

